BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:project-100-exhibition-residencies-2027-nelson@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123741Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Project 100: Exhibition Residencies 2027 for Curators and
  Recent Graduates (Whakatu Nelson)
DESCRIPTION:Project 100\, an artist-run contemporary gallery and project sp
 ace in Whakatu Nelson\, is programming its 2027 exhibition residencies in 
 two streams. RECENT GRADUATES EXHIBITION RESIDENCY (May 2027): open to art
 ists who graduated from a tertiary arts programme within the past two year
 s\, preferably from a New Zealand institution\, and who can independently 
 realise an exhibition or public programme off a strong conceptual proposal
 . CURATORS EXHIBITION RESIDENCY (November 2027): open to emerging and esta
 blished curators\, independent practitioners and collectives based in Aote
 aroa New Zealand\; previous curatorial experience is welcomed but not esse
 ntial. Solo and collaborative projects are both welcome. WHAT YOU GET: exc
 lusive use of the gallery for one month\, one month of accommodation in a 
 central-city apartment\, administrative and promotional support\, up to fo
 ur hours of technician support\, and a travel and food stipend of up to NZ
 $1\,000. The gallery takes no commission on sales. WHAT YOU BRING: residen
 ts run the gallery themselves\, keep it open during opening hours\, must b
 e based in Whakatu Nelson for the month\, and return the space to its orig
 inal condition. Note this is an exhibition residency for presenting an exh
 ibition or public programme\, not a studio residency for developing new wo
 rk\, though some practices can work from the gallery during the exhibition
 . A refundable NZ$400 exhibition bond is paid once you are selected and re
 turned after the exhibition. DEADLINE CONFLICT\, CHECK BEFORE APPLYING: Pr
 oject 100's own application guide (the updated curators and grads residenc
 y PDF linked from its proposals page) states applications close 31 August\
 , while the open-call listings carrying this residency state 14 September 
 2026 at midnight. Email Project 100 to confirm which applies before assumi
 ng the call is still open. Apply via the form on the Project 100 proposals
  page.\n\nOrganisation: Project 100\nLocation: Project 100 gallery\, Whaka
 tu Nelson\, Aotearoa New Zealand. Open to curators\, recent graduates and 
 collectives based in Aotearoa New Zealand\; residents must be in Whakatu N
 elson for the full month.\nAward: Travel and food stipend of up to NZ$1\,0
 00\, plus one month of exclusive use of the Project 100 gallery\, one mont
 h of accommodation in a central-city apartment\, administrative and promot
 ional support (including national promotion through Art Now)\, and up to f
 our hours of technician support. No commission is taken on sales. No appli
 cation fee\, but a refundable NZ$400 exhibition bond is paid by the select
 ed artist and returned once the exhibition wraps up.\nDuration: One month.
  Recent Graduates residency runs May 2027\; Curators residency runs Novemb
 er 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.project100.co.nz/takeoverthespace?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.project100.co.nz/takeoverthespace?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Project 100 gallery\, Whakatu Nelson\, Aotearoa New Zealand. Open 
 to curators\, recent graduates and collectives based in Aotearoa New Zeala
 nd\; residents must be in Whakatu Nelson for the full month.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bigci-environmental-awards-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123741Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:Deadline: BigCi Environmental Awards 2026
DESCRIPTION:BigCi's Environmental Awards are an annual prize for work that 
 engages with the environment\, open to Australian and international artist
 s working in visual art\, installation\, multimedia\, performance\, litera
 ture\, music\, photography\, filmmaking and curating. TWO WINNERS each rec
 eive four weeks of free residency at BigCi plus AUD 5\,000 in prize money.
  BigCi sits on the edge of Wollemi National Park in the Greater Blue Mount
 ains\, an hour and a half from Sydney but geologically another world\; win
 ners explore the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Wollemi\, Blue Mountains and
  Gardens of Stone National Parks on guided walks and are given research as
 sistance relevant to their projects. At the end of their residencies they 
 present the work at the BigCi Open Day. JUDGING: three independent judges\
 , Lea Kannar-Lichtenberger (Australia)\, Brian Wallace (China) and Dan Got
 tlieb (USA). APPLICATION: an online submission form (Wufoo) linked from th
 e awards page\, with a non-refundable AUD 40 entry fee paid at the time of
  submission. KEY DATES: submissions close 2 August 2026\; winners announce
 d 22 August 2026. Enquiries via the contact form at bigci.org/contact.\n\n
 Organisation: Bilpin International Ground for Creative Initiatives (BigCi)
 \nLocation: Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi 
 National Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\,
  about 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists
 .\nAward: Two awards\, each of AUD 5\,000 prize money plus four weeks of f
 ree residency at BigCi\, guided walks in the surrounding national parks an
 d research assistance for the project. AUD 40 entry fee\, non-refundable a
 nd payable with the submission.\nDuration: Four-week residency at BigCi pe
 r winner\n\nMore: https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi Nati
 onal Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\, abo
 ut 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists.
END:VEVENT
